feat(mcp): add describe_workspace (#205)

Driven by MCP-039..MCP-043, written first and observed failing twice: once
with no tool to call at all, then against a stub that answered nothing, so
every row failed for the reason doc 07 names rather than for a missing
symbol. MCP-043 is the strongest of the five -- it runs the reference
shim's own derive_task beside the Go for every branch shape the shell
covers and refuses a disagreement, which is how the greedy RM match, the
throwaway worktree-agent branch, the unborn branch and the detached HEAD
were settled by measurement instead of by reading.

The derivation is the shim's, moved: the main worktree resolves the
repository, the branch is the one THIS tree's commits land on, the task is
the RM number the branch carries or the branch folded into doc 02 5's
grammar, and repo comes from origin through event.ValidateRepo -- never
synthesised from a directory name.

The one new deployment value is INNSEGL_HOST_PROJECTS, written from the
same INNSEGL_PROJECTS the mount is written from so the two cannot drift.
Unset, outside the mount, or not a working tree, the tool refuses with its
own message and an existing IP 4 class. A guessed translation describes the
wrong repository confidently, and the answer is on its way into an
append-only record.

One refusal the shim does not have: a linked worktree that is not under its
repository. The shim left that relative path empty, and sign_commit reads
an empty worktree as the repository itself (MCP-029), so an empty answer
would send the next call to a different tree.

100% statement coverage on internal/mcp, every error path included.

